{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>A song of ascents. I rejoiced when they said</b> — Rabbi Moses said: David composed this song to be sung with the praises in the House of HaShem at the time the House would be built. And Rabbi Yeshuah said: This is on account of the House that David established for himself in Zion. And some say: Concerning the Third House — each one of Israel says: <b>I rejoiced when they said</b> — they are the pilgrims."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 122, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:10.760066102Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}